  "question": {
    "text": "The value of $\\int_0^{\\infty} \\frac{d x}{\\left(x^2+4\\right)\\left(x^2+9\\right)}$ is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{\\pi}{60}$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{\\pi}{20}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{\\pi}{40}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{\\pi}{80}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\text { Hints : } \\left.\\int_0^{\\infty} \\frac{\\mathrm{dx}}{\\left(\\mathrm{x}^2+4\\right)\\left(\\mathrm{x}^2+9\\right)}=\\int_0^{\\pi / 2} \\frac{\\sec ^2 \\theta}{\\left(\\tan ^2 \\theta+4\\right)\\left(\\tan ^2 \\theta+9\\right)} \\mathrm{d} \\theta \\text { (putting } \\mathrm{x}=\\tan \\theta\\right) \\\\\n& =\\frac{1}{5} \\int_0^{\\pi / 2} \\frac{\\left\\{\\left(9+\\tan ^2 \\theta\\right)-\\left(4+\\tan ^2 \\theta\\right)\\right\\} \\sec ^2 \\theta}{\\left(\\tan ^2 \\theta+4\\right)\\left(\\tan ^2 \\theta+9\\right)} \\mathrm{d} \\theta\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n=\\frac{1}{5}\\left[\\int_0^{\\pi / 2} \\frac{\\sec ^2 \\theta}{4+\\tan ^2 \\theta} \\mathrm{d} \\theta-\\int_0^{\\pi / 2} \\frac{\\sec ^2 \\theta}{9+\\tan ^2 \\theta} \\mathrm{d} \\theta\\right]\n$$\n\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& =\\frac{1}{5}\\left[\\left.\\frac{1}{2} \\tan ^{-1}\\left(\\frac{\\tan \\theta}{2}\\right)\\right|_0 ^{\\pi / 2}-\\left.\\frac{1}{3} \\tan ^{-1}\\left(\\frac{\\tan \\theta}{3}\\right)\\right|_0 ^{\\pi / 2}\\right] \\\\\n& =\\frac{1}{5}\\left[\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{\\pi}{2}-\\frac{1}{3} \\cdot \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right]=\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)\\left(\\frac{1}{5}\\right)\\left(\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{3}\\right)=\\frac{\\pi}{2} \\cdot \\frac{1}{5} \\cdot \\frac{1}{6}=\\frac{\\pi}{60}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"
